-- R3's third way out: bridge at the call.
--
-- Two sibling sections each declare `foo`. A rule under one of them calls a
-- rule under the other, and says "my foo is yours, for this call". That is the
-- remedy `doc/reference/syntax/section-given.md` offers alongside hoisting the
-- binder and renaming one of them.
--
-- The name to the LEFT of IS is one of the CALLEE's implicit inputs, so it is
-- matched against what the callee reads, the same way a declared parameter's
-- name is. The expression to the right is ordinary, and resolves here.

§ `1`
    GIVEN foo IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 4

GIVETH A NUMBER
f MEANS g WITH foo IS foo

§ `2`
    GIVEN foo IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 99

GIVETH A NUMBER
g MEANS foo TIMES 10

-- 40: section 1's foo reached g. Not 990, which is what g gets on its own.
#EVAL f
#EVAL g

#ASSERT f EQUALS 40
#ASSERT g EQUALS 990
